      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to calculate the number of days between these two dates and find the corresponding day of the week.\n\nFirst, let's find the total number of days between November 23 and December 23:\n- November has 30 days, so from November 23 to November 30 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days.\n- December has 23 days, so there are 23 days from December 1 to December 23, inclusive.\n- Therefore, the total number of days between November 23 and December 23 is \\(8 + 23 = 31\\) days.\n\nNext, we need to determine how many days past Thanksgiving November 23 is:\n- November has 30 days, so November 23 is the 23rd day of the month.\n- Subtracting November 23 from November 30 gives 8 days.\n- Since November has 30 days, November 23 is the 23rd day of November, which is 3 days past the 20th day of November.\n- Therefore, November 23 is the 23rd day of November, which is 23 - 3 = 20 days after the 27th day (which is after Thanksgiving).\n\nSince Thanksgiving is on the 27th day of October, the calculation is straightforward because we adjust for the exact day:\n- November 23 is 23 days into November, which is 3 days past Thanksgiving.\n- Therefore, December 23 is \\(23 - 3 = 20\\) days after Monday (when Thanksgiving is).\n\nTo find the day of the week for December 23, we need to count 20 days from Monday:\n\\[ 20 \\div 7 = 2 \\text{ R } 6 \\]\nThis means 20 days is equivalent to 2 weeks and 6 days. Starting from Monday, adding 6 days gives us the day of the week for December 23:\n\\[ \\text{Monday} + 6 \\text{ days} = \\text{Sunday} \\]\n\nTherefore, December 23 is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\).",
